ui/dbus-clipboard: forward grabs and complete requests from a serial-less agent

The Windows spice vd_agent (0.10.0, and master as of 2026-09) never announces
VD_AGENT_CAP_CLIPBOARD_GRAB_SERIAL, so ui/vdagent.c builds its grab infos with
has_serial = false.  dbus_clipboard_update_info() then returned before either
forwarding the guest's Grab to the D-Bus client or completing the client's
pending Request with the data the agent had already delivered -- the request
simply timed out after 5 s.  Host-to-guest worked; guest-to-host could not, on
any Windows guest.  Pass serial 0 for such agents: qemu_clipboard_check_serial()
already treats a serial-less info as always current.

Observed on QEMU 10.2.1 / Windows 11 with virtio-win 0.1.285's vdagent
(caps 0x46B7).  See docs/plans/windows-home-vm.md, Results, experiment 6.

--- a/ui/dbus-clipboard.c
+++ b/ui/dbus-clipboard.c
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ dbus_clipboard_update_info(DBusDisplay *dpy, QemuClipboardInfo *info)
         return;
     }
 
-    if (self_update || !info->has_serial) {
+    if (self_update) {
         return;
     }
 
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@ dbus_clipboard_update_info(DBusDisplay *dpy, QemuClipboardInfo *info)
             qemu_dbus_display1_clipboard_call_grab(
                 dpy->clipboard_proxy,
                 info->selection,
-                info->serial,
+                info->has_serial ? info->serial : 0,
                 mime,
                 G_DBUS_CALL_FLAGS_NONE, -1, NULL, NULL, NULL);
         }
